.TH LUCERNACTL 1 "@DATE@" "Lucerna @VERSION@" "Lucerna"
.SH NAME
lucernactl \- control the Lucerna wallpaper service from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lucernactl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lucernactl
talks to the running
.BR lucernad (1)
over the session D-Bus. It works without a graphical session and never plays wallpapers itself.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show what the service is doing.
.TP
.B monitors \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List the detected monitors and their stable ids (alias:
.BR displays ).
.TP
.B wallpapers \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List the wallpaper library.
.TP
.B play \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-monitor \fIid\fR]
Add a video or animated image to the library and play it, on all monitors or on one (a monitor id
or a connector name such as HDMI-1).
.TP
.B pause
Pause all wallpapers.
.TP
.B resume
Resume after
.BR pause .
.TP
.B stop \fR[\fB\-\-daemon\fR]
Stop all wallpapers; with
.B \-\-daemon
ask the service itself to quit.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read the configuration and start over.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-redact\fR]
Gather everything needed to debug desktop integration. Works even if the service is not running.
.B \-\-redact
hides the home directory, user name, host name, wallpaper file names and monitor serial numbers.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
The service is not running.
.TP
.B 4
Bad request (unknown wallpaper or display, bad path).
.TP
.B 5
Unsupported session (for example Wayland).
.TP
.B 6
Configuration problem.
.TP
.B 7
mpv is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lucerna (1),
.BR lucernad (1)
